course: dictionary
lesson: 11679
title: Astonishment: a very big surprise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Astonishment is a feeling of very great surprise. It is bigger than being a little surprised. Look at the words around it for clues. «She stood frozen in astonishment as the lights came on by themselves.» Frozen and stood still show that she was very surprised.
explain: Astonishment is a noun, a name for a feeling. People often show it with their bodies: they gasp, stare or freeze. Useful phrases are «in astonishment» and «to my astonishment», which means something surprised me very much.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «a feeling of very great surprise». «He stared at the rabbit in astonishment» becomes «He stared at the rabbit in a feeling of very great surprise». It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Astonishment means a feeling of very great surprise.
fact: Astonishment is a noun, a name for a feeling.
fact: Phrases to know: «in astonishment», «stare in astonishment», «to my astonishment».
fact: «To my astonishment» means something surprised me very much, as in «To my astonishment, the cat opened the fridge».
fact: In Alice, Alice is often filled with astonishment at Wonderland.
exercise: «She stared at the talking cat in astonishment.» What does astonishment mean here? | *Feeling of very great surprise | A loud noise | Feeling of being very tired | Feeling cold and wet
exercise: Which word could replace astonishment in «Her mouth fell open in astonishment»? | *Surprise | Tiredness | Boredom | Fear
exercise: Which action shows astonishment? | *Gasping and staring with wide eyes | Eating a sandwich slowly | Yawning and closing your eyes | Whistling a happy tune
test: «To my astonishment, the library was open on Sunday.» What does «to my astonishment» show? | I was very hungry | *I was very surprised | I was very bored | I was very sleepy
test: Which sentence uses astonishment correctly? | *He stared at the bird in astonishment | He stared at the bird astonishments | He stared at the bird in an astonishments | He astonishment the bird
exam: Read: «The crowd fell silent in astonishment as the magician vanished.» What is the crowd feeling? | Angry | *Very surprised | Hungry | Sleepy
